---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import HeroText from "../components/HeroText.astro";

const metadata = {
  siteTitle: "Seaside Heritage Network",
  pageTitle: "Accessibility Statement",
  description:
    "How accessible the Seaside Heritage Network website is, and how to get help if you have trouble using it.",
};

const proseClass =
  "prose prose-headings:font-heading prose-headings:font-medium prose-h2:text-3xl prose-h2:text-[var(--shn-color-bg-page)] prose-h2:scroll-mt-24 prose-p:text-gray-700 prose-li:text-gray-700 prose-ul:list-disc prose-ul:list-outside prose-ul:pl-5 [&_li::marker]:text-gray-700 prose-a:text-[var(--shn-color-primary)] prose-a:underline-offset-2 hover:prose-a:text-accent max-w-3xl";
---

<PageLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <HeroText
    title="Accessibility Statement"
    subtitle="How accessible the Seaside Heritage Network website is, and how to get help if you have trouble using it."
  />

  <section class="bg-stone-100 text-dark">
    <div
      class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:flex lg:justify-center"
    >
      <article class={proseClass}>
        <p>
          We want everyone to be able to use the Seaside Heritage Network
          website, whatever their needs. This statement explains how accessible
          the site is, where we know it falls short, and how to get help.
        </p>

        <h2 id="our-aim">Our aim</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to meet the{" "}
          <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2</a
          >{" "}
          at level AA. We're a small, volunteer-run charity, and while we've worked
          hard on accessibility, we know some parts of the site don't fully meet this
          standard yet. These are listed below.
        </p>

        <h2 id="what-weve-done">What we've done</h2>
        <p>You should be able to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            navigate the whole site using only a keyboard, with a clear visible
            focus showing where you are
          </li>
          <li>
            use a "skip to main content" link to jump past the menu on every
            page
          </li>
          <li>
            navigate using a screen reader, with pages organised into clear
            regions and headings in a logical order
          </li>
          <li>
            zoom in up to 400% without content being cut off, and use the site
            on a phone or tablet
          </li>
          <li>
            understand images through text descriptions, with decorative images
            hidden from screen readers
          </li>
          <li>
            filter and search the Resource Hub using a keyboard or screen reader
          </li>
          <li>
            play videos using a proper labelled play button, with a written
            summary of each resource on the page itself
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We also run automated accessibility tests on the site as part of our
          regular development work.
        </p>

        <h2 id="known-issues">Known issues</h2>
        <p>We know some parts of the site aren't fully accessible:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Some PDFs aren't fully accessible.</strong> A few older documents,
            such as our commissioned walking trail guides, weren't created to work
            well with screen readers. The key information from each one is summarised
            on its resource page, and we can provide the content in another format
            on request.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Walking trail videos don't have audio description.</strong>
            These short videos are set to music, with no narration, and are there
            to give a flavour of the trail. All the important information is in the
            text on the same page.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong
              >Captions on our recorded seminars are generated automatically by
              YouTube</strong
            > and may contain mistakes.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong
              >Some services we link to are run by other organisations.</strong
            > Event booking (TicketSource), our newsletter sign-up (Brevo) and Bucket
            &amp; Spade List voting (Microsoft Forms) aren't under our control, and
            their accessibility may vary.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="reporting-a-problem">
          Asking for another format or reporting a problem
        </h2>
        <p>
          If you need any content in a different format, such as accessible PDF,
          large print or plain text, or if you find something on the site that's
          difficult to use, please email us at{" "}
          <a href="mailto:info@seasideheritage.org.uk">
            info@seasideheritage.org.uk
          </a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Please tell us the page or document you're having trouble with, and
          what would help. We'll aim to reply within{" "}
          <mark class="bg-pink-100 text-pink-700 px-1 rounded not-prose"
            >[5 working days]</mark
          >.
        </p>
        <p>
          We're a small volunteer team, so we can't always fix things straight
          away, but we'll always look at what we can do.
        </p>

        <h2 id="how-we-tested">How we tested this site</h2>
        <p>
          This site was last tested on{" "}
          <mark class="bg-pink-100 text-pink-700 px-1 rounded not-prose"
            >[date]</mark
          >. We tested it using:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            automated accessibility testing (axe) across our main types of page
          </li>
          <li>keyboard-only navigation</li>
          <li>
            the VoiceOver screen reader on{" "}
            <mark class="bg-pink-100 text-pink-700 px-1 rounded not-prose"
              >[Mac/iPhone]</mark
            >
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="keeping-up-to-date">Keeping this statement up to date</h2>
        <p>
          We'll review this statement at least once a year, and whenever we add
          significant new features to the site.
        </p>
        <p>
          This statement was prepared on{" "}
          <mark class="bg-pink-100 text-pink-700 px-1 rounded not-prose"
            >[date]</mark
          >. It was last reviewed on{" "}
          <mark class="bg-pink-100 text-pink-700 px-1 rounded not-prose"
            >[date]</mark
          >.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
